WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.960 line:80%
Live technical data passes
through a message broker.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.350 line:80%
A separate Node service forwards it
to React through Socket.IO.

00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:12.693 line:80%
The original interface runs locally
against a local broker;

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:15.353 line:80%
synthetic messages then
update the pressure

00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:18.163 line:80%
charts through the real messaging path.

00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:23.684 line:80%
Station records and source
configuration follow another path,

00:00:23.694 --> 00:00:26.194 line:80%
through Express and MongoDB.

00:00:26.897 --> 00:00:31.727 line:80%
A separate Python processor turns
spreadsheets into JSON reports.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:36.117 line:80%
Importing those results into application
records is a separate step.

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:42.247 line:80%
Container definitions and deployment
files document the intended topology.

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:45.697 line:80%
A working deployment still
needs separate verification.

00:00:46.381 --> 00:00:49.891 line:80%
Three paths, three boundaries:
live messages,

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:53.011 line:80%
application records and file processing.

00:00:53.021 --> 00:00:55.201 line:80%
The inspected version forwards live

00:00:55.381 --> 00:00:58.821 line:80%
messages without saving every update
to the database.
